## Walkthrough 

The flag is in the image resources `sonnet.xml`, `cadence.xml`, `lyra.xml`, `arya.xml` and `tempo.xml`. These have characters in purple and green, but the purple background hides the flag. You have to change the background color to any other color to view the purple text. 

If you look at `FrameActivity.kt`, you'll notice that if `rightPitch` is `true` the background color is set to `#8DC63F`, which will hide the green text and only show the purple text. 

## Using Frida

To set-up Frida on your laptop,

````
pip3 install frida-tools
````

To figure out the architecture of the emulator image,

````
adb shell getprop ro.product.cpu.abi
````

Then download the corresponding `frida-server` from [Github](https://github.com/frida/frida/release). Then copy the Frida server to the emulator and start it.

````
adb root
adb push <path_to_frida_server> /data/local/tmp/frida-server
adb shell chmod 755 /data/local/tmp/frida-server
adb shell /data/local/tmp/frida-server &
frida -U -f com.bsidessf.doremi -l hook.js
````

I used Pixel 6 Android 13.0 build, with Api 33. In order to use adb root, you need to use a non-production Android build i.e., a Google APIs build vs. a Google Play build.

## Using APKtool 

`java -jar apktool_2.12.1.jar doremi.apk` 

Pull the files `sonnet.xml`, `cadence.xml`, `lyra.xml`, `arya.xml` and `tempo.xml` from `res/drawable`. 

You can use `python3 solution.py` to create `combined.svg` with the flag. 


